    "interpretation": "in_domain_* results show what accuracy this feature representation/classifier achieves when train and test come from the same source. kaggle_to_webcam and webcam_to_kaggle show what happens when the model has never seen the OTHER source at all. A large drop from in-domain to cross-domain accuracy is evidence of genuine domain shift (capture device / lighting / temporal smoothing / detection-threshold differences), not of the model failing to learn the sign shapes themselves."
