    "caveat": "Handedness here is inferred from which hand-feature block is non-zero at capture time, not ground-truth sign linguistics (some classes are inherently one-handed signs; this mixes 'sign is one-handed' with 'only one hand was detected'). A single classifier trained on the full mixed-handedness training set is evaluated separately on each test subset, so this measures whether ONE model generalizes evenly across handedness conditions, not whether per-handedness specialist models would do better."
  },
